2026-08-25T20:50:07Z	tried	what=the supervisor reloads job.rec every pass	config=each pass re-reads the spec; a bad spec keeps the running config; a changed worker_cmd is refused as needing a stand-down	produced=two reloads observed live under a running supervisor: bank_s 600->660 at 20:48:05 and 660->600 at 20:49:06, both journalled; a deliberately broken spec left the supervisor alive and sampling	claim=MEASURED	control=the broken-spec arm is the control that matters — without it, 'reloads the config' is indistinguishable from 'crashes on any edit', and the reload would be worse than the snapshot it replaced	why=I tightened bank_s, banked it, and reported it done while the running supervisor kept the old value: it had snapshotted the config at startup. Third instance in two days of 'the thing running is not the thing you edited' — stale binary, stale config, and a grep that lied about a binary. On this project the thing editing job.rec is a woken heartbeat agent with no reason to suspect any of that.	node=119098
